From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:48:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 52/56] Paste a copied column block as a block at the cursor

Text copied or cut from a column block pasted at a plain cursor went in
as ordinary lines, splitting the line at the cursor. As in Notepad++, it
now goes in as a block: each row at the cursor's column on the lines
below, short lines padded with spaces, rows past the end of the file on
new lines, as one undo step. The app remembers the last column copy, so
anything copied elsewhere since still pastes normally.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/column_select.rs b/src/column_select.rs
index c919c28..eb1f42d 100644
--- a/src/column_select.rs
+++ b/src/column_select.rs
@@ -295,6 +295,78 @@ pub fn paste<'buffer, E: Edit<'buffer>>(
